  "question": {
    "text": "Let P be the parabola, whose focus is $(-2,1)$ and directrix is $2 x+y+2=0$. Then the sum of the ordinates of the points on P , whose abscissa is -2 , is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GTU3G",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "isctk",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WDy4e",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Sucse",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of parabola<br/>$(x+2)^2+(y-1)^2=\\left(\\frac{2 x+y+2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right)^2$<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/qZ3Y8sfiWupYB2A7M7C8hxcWRQvBpUEFE3t7VgevHOM.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$5\\left[(x+2)^2+(y-1)^2\\right]=(2 x+y+2)^2$<br/>Put $x=-2,5(y-1)^2=(y-2)^2$<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& 5\\left(y^2-2 y+1\\right)=y^2-4 y+4 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 4 y^2-6 y+1=0 \\Rightarrow y_1+y_2=\\frac{3}{2}<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
